A71: more processes can get a Metal device, and refusals are logged. Only backboardd and the names in
extra_client() (AegirPoster, MercuryPosterExtension, PosterBoard) may open the GPU; everyone else got
kIOReturnNotPrivileged silently. On iOS 26 the "Clear" home screen icons come out as empty glass and widgets
as blank white tiles, and SpringBoard logs "native A618 backend unavailable"; which process renders them is
not known, so:
- every refused process is logged twice: "SWEET RENDER: NAME refused: not a Metal client";
- sweetmtlextra=NAME[,NAME...] adds names to the list without a kernel build;
- sweetm2window=128 makes each extra client window 128 MiB instead of 256 MiB, so 6 extra slots fit in the
  same 0x80000000..0xb0000000 range (0xb0000000.. stays the framebuffer present-copy range); sweetm2extra
  still lowers the count. Defaults are unchanged (3 slots of 256 MiB, same names).

